{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwSh1QR99hqhHyanoza2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. Its status is still \"pending\", because it hasn't run yet. I didn't open the dashboard to check how the panels render.\n\n**What the data holds:** The Kibana Sample Data Logs view covers web-server requests. The fields I used are `timestamp`, `response` (a string field, so values like \"503\"), `bytes`, `extension`, `clientip` and `geo.*`. The rest are `machine.os`, `agent`, `referer`, `url` and `request`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-ef306c8c Web logs overview\" (id `eff-ef306c8c-web-logs-overview-557467553fa5`), with a default range of the last 7 days. It has four panels:\n- Total requests, as a single number.\n- Requests over time, as a line chart.\n- Responses by status code, as a pie chart.\n- Bytes by file extension, as a bar chart.\n\n**Alert rule:** \"EFF-ef306c8c 5xx spike\" (id `d2a727f4-a05e-4251-b894-ae0dfcb6ba01`) is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`. It runs every minute and counts documents whose `response.keyword` starts with \"5\" over the last 5 minutes. It fires when that count is above 10. Because there is no action connector, it only records alerts in Kibana and won't send a notification."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1262,"cache_read_input_tokens":19094,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1262},"output_tokens":471,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"64586df7-e9b4-4a2e-a3c1-a2cdab6c3197","timestamp":"2026-10-12T01:04:26.621Z","request_id":"req_011CfwSh1BmoA8Mpn2JFJsj7"}
